course: dictionary
lesson: 6437
title: Na: one short word, several jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The same short word can mean different things in different places. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «I'm na going.» In Scottish talk, na means not, so the sentence says I am not going.
explain: «Na, I'm fine.» Here na is casual slang for no, the friendly way people say it in chats and everyday talk. The words around it show that someone is turning down an offer or answering a question.
explain: Na is also a science symbol. Na is the chemical symbol for sodium, a soft silvery metal found in salt, and NaCl is table salt. The symbol comes from the old Latin name natrium.
explain: Na is also the end of words like «gonna» (going to) and «wanna» (want to), where speech is clipped. Be careful: N/A on a form means not applicable, which is a different thing.
fact: Na is a short word with several meanings, so check the context before you decide.
fact: In Scottish and Northern English, «na» means «not» or «no», as in «I'm na going».
fact: In casual speech and chats, «na» or «nah» is a relaxed way to say «no».
fact: Na is the chemical symbol for sodium, a soft silvery metal found in salt.
fact: «Gonna» and «wanna» end with na, short for going to and want to.
exercise: In Scotland a friend says, «I'm na going to the party.» What does na mean here? | Yes, very much | Tomorrow | *Not | Maybe
exercise: In a chat, someone asks, «Want to play?» and you reply, «Na, I'm fine.» What does na mean? | *No | Happy | Please | Wait
exercise: On a science chart, the symbol Na stands for which element? | Gold | Iron | *Sodium
test: In «gonna» and «wanna», what do the letters na stand for? | Not and no | Nature and nurse | *Going to and want to | Table salt and sodium
test: What is true about N/A on a form? | *It means not applicable | It is a Scottish word for not | It is slang for no | It is the same as Na for sodium
exam: A text says, «Na, I'm na going, and the salt is NaCl.» Which two meanings of na are used? | Chlorine and gold | *No or not, and sodium | Sodium and going to | Not applicable and table salt
